{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular floor measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> feet, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18850c5a6f67139956c8c1e35094c0a864ecb8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. An artist paints a rectangle on the floor with the sides of the rectangle parallel to the sides of the floor. The unpainted part of the floor forms a border of width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot around the painted rectangle and occupies half of the area of the entire floor. How many possibilities are there for the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9959d47fffb760b6cf89894df252b99436e4d8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fed69843311a5e5216d87e85fe02feac60a5d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{outer}=ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c33579cbe80bd0e5bd3415ba477b4caa17935b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{inner}=(a-2)(b-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757c962ba6ebb6e9ad18ac6a2ee5c1ffd1e162c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{outer}=2A_{inner}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b925e74f1354017676a76257486639387f9ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=2(a-2)(b-2)=2ab-4a-4b+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff18e6eb0f9a8e0219403005539eb6477d214cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0=ab-4a-4b+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>By Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682a01457c9addb2ee8ad8c70cfa3948b30c2a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8=ab-4a-4b+16=(a-4)(b-4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9627c731ffbdf790e34a767c172cc85661cc20e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8=1\\times8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3ca5723cc6684d22228499b8dd4b117e66b0504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8=2\\times4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> are the only positive factorings of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f48773d0453ebdf4578b43503eb2c8f3dbb9219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)=(5,12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b7955dbde20972bec72a6d2d6ba9f11fb41d9ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)=(6,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/92582466d4e1ab0c4d7745fc87114975cd3517b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions. Notice that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, the reversed pairs are invalid.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> 